        HelpEntry(
            id = "watch",
            title = "Galaxy Watch",
            keywords = listOf("watch app", "my watch", "wear os", "watch tile", "complication"),
            what = "Navilife on your Galaxy Watch: Up next with Done, quick capture by voice, a tile and a complication.",
            how = "Open Navilife on the watch and enter the code it shows under Settings → Watch.",
            tips = listOf("The watch syncs on its own, it isn't a remote screen for the phone.", "On a Barça match day the watch shows the match from an hour before kick-off (when and where it's on), then the live score and the last goal, then full time; the tile says the same in one line and, while it's on, the complication's ring is the score. Each goal's buzz is the phone's heads-up on your wrist.", "Before a meeting with other people the watch shows the prep too, from the lead time you set in Mail until ten minutes after the start: when it starts, who's coming and the one or two most useful lines (their last email, what's open, when you last met); the tile says it in one line.", "With no signal the watch keeps what you tap (Done, captures, a fast) and sends it when it's back online; the foot of its screen says \"Offline · your changes here wait to sync\" and the tile says \"Waiting to sync\" until they've gone.", "To unlink the watch from the watch itself, scroll to the foot of its screen and tap Unlink this watch, then Unlink: it needs a connection, sends what's waiting first, then forgets your day and shows a new code. You can also unlink it from Settings → Watch on the phone or the Mac.", "The watch keeps Navilife's quiet hours (Settings → Notifications): its screen and tile say \"Quiet hours · until 07:00\", the tile leaves out the inbox count till morning, and to save battery it syncs about hourly and refreshes less often overnight. A parking timer, a meeting about to start or a live match still count down as usual."),
